{"name":"Husky Orange","hex":"#bb613e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"husky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a voice, hoarse and rough-sounding; throaty.","Burly, stout; sometimes as a modifier for boys' clothing sizes that fit a large waist or chest."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several breeds of dogs used as sled dogs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/husky"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Husky","blocks":[{"text":"Husky is a general term for a type of dog used in the polar regions, primarily and specifically for work as sled dogs. It also refers to a traditional northern type, notable for its cold-weather tolerance and overall hardiness. Modern racing huskies that maintain arctic breed traits represent an ever-changing crossbreed of the fastest dogs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Huskiesatrest.jpg/330px-Huskiesatrest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husky","wikidata":"Q3244349"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/DOG-HUSKY_23JUL00.jpg/500px-DOG-HUSKY_23JUL00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/DOG-HUSKY_23JUL00.jpg/500px-DOG-HUSKY_23JUL00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Siberian Husky with heterochromia ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADOG-HUSKY_23JUL00.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Three_inuit_men_feeding_Labrador_huskies_in_Nain%2C_Canada.jpg/500px-Three_inuit_men_feeding_Labrador_huskies_in_Nain%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Three_inuit_men_feeding_Labrador_huskies_in_Nain%2C_Canada.jpg/500px-Three_inuit_men_feeding_Labrador_huskies_in_Nain%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Labrador Huskies being fed by Inuit men","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThree_inuit_men_feeding_Labrador_huskies_in_Nain%2C_Canada.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Alaskan_husky_%281815096882%29.jpg/500px-Alaskan_husky_%281815096882%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Alaskan_husky_%281815096882%29.jpg/1280px-Alaskan_husky_%281815096882%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Alaskan_husky_%281815096882%29.jpg